  "id": "alpha-neurofeedback",
  "term": "alpha neurofeedback",
  "definition": "Alpha neurofeedback is a form of neurofeedback training that uses EEG signals related to alpha brain-wave activity, especially the upper alpha range, to try to increase a person’s alpha amplitude. It has been studied as a possible way to influence cognitive abilities such as short-term memory, although the provided source notes mixed findings about effects on cognitive performance.",
